    <p class="lede first reveal">The fantasy is a beach and a phone that pings with sales while you do nothing. It's a good fantasy, and it has sold a lot of courses. It's also the single biggest reason people quit before passive income ever works — because the fantasy skips the only part that matters.</p>
    <p class="reveal">Real passive income is not effort-free. It's effort-shifted. You do the work once, up front, and it keeps paying afterward — which is a very different thing from work that never happens. The beach is real. The "doing nothing" that supposedly built it is not.</p>
    <p class="reveal"><strong>You do not have a passive income problem. You have a sequencing problem.</strong> The question was never "how do I earn without working" — it's "what do I build first, so that later it earns without me?" Get the order right and passive income stops being a fantasy and starts being a schedule.</p>

