    <div class="chapter left reveal"><span class="bignum">02</span><div class="num">Chapter Two</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="counts">What actually counts as a passive stream</h2></div>
    <p class="answer reveal">The passive income streams that work for a faceless business are digital products, affiliate content, and anything you build once that keeps being found — because the asset does the selling long after you've made it.</p>
    <p class="reveal">The test is simple: does it keep earning when you stop touching it? A digital product on a checkout link does. An evergreen article with affiliate links does. A service you personally deliver does not — the moment you stop, the income stops. <strong>Passive means the asset works when you don't.</strong></p>

