    <div class="chapter reveal"><div class="num">Answered</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="faq">Frequently asked</h2></div>
    <h3 class="reveal">Is passive income actually passive?</h3>
    <p class="reveal">Not in the building. Passive income is money that keeps coming after the work is done — but the work is real and front-loaded. A better word is "leveraged": you make one piece of work pay more than once, which is very different from work that never happens.</p>
    <h3 class="reveal">What's the best passive income stream for a beginner?</h3>
    <p class="reveal">A single digital product. It's the fastest asset to build, sells on a checkout link with no audience, and teaches you the whole model in one cycle. Start with one, finished, before you stack anything on top.</p>
    <h3 class="reveal">How long until passive income actually pays?</h3>
    <p class="reveal">Expect a lag, often months, between building an asset and seeing it earn meaningfully — especially when the traffic is evergreen search that compounds over time. The wait is the real cost; consistency through the quiet stretch is what separates the people it works for.</p>

